    RESOLVED (2026-08-19): the original 73-card Conversation Types download pass failed silently (root cause found on retry, NOT a Chrome permissions issue as first guessed) — Canva's "Download" menu item is asynchronous: clicking it shows a brief loading-spinner while the file is generated server-side, and the actual browser download only fires after that. The original automation clicked "Next" immediately after "Download" in the same step, canceling every in-flight download before it completed. Fix: always click "Download" via a fresh element reference (never a reused pixel coordinate — Canva's menu position drifts slightly between renders), then issue a separate explicit wait (~4s) before doing anything else, and verify the file landed on disk before advancing to the next card.
    All 73 Conversation Types images (74 files counting the confirmed true duplicate C-Welcoming3.7.png) were successfully redownloaded using this fixed pattern and delivered to the Mac as 5 zip parts (CT-p1.zip .. CT-p5.zip) inside /Users/office/School-of-Conscious-Communication/Conversation Types/. THESE STILL NEED TO BE UNZIPPED (into that same folder, then the 5 .zip files deleted) — this session doesn't have shell access to the user's Mac (device_bash unavailable), so unzip must be done manually (double-click each in Finder) or by a future session that has device_bash access.

    All 91 Choice Lens images were downloaded using the same proven pattern (mostly via a subagent that ground through
    the per-card find->click->wait sequence) and delivered to the Mac as 5 zip parts (CL-p1.zip .. CL-p5.zip) inside
    /Users/office/School-of-Conscious-Communication/Choice Lenses/. THESE STILL NEED TO BE UNZIPPED, same as above.

    Discovered this session: switching a Canva folder to Grid view renders each thumbnail large enough to read the
    card's "Definition:" text directly (zoom into the thumbnail), which is much faster for transcription than opening
    each card's individual preview. Used for Choice Lens; worth using again for Value Lens.

    Also discovered: a Canva folder's single-image preview page (opened by clicking a thumbnail) has a "Next" arrow
    that pages through every file in the folder without returning to the list view — reusable for the download loop
    (find "..." -> Download -> wait 4s -> find "Next" -> repeat) without re-navigating each time.

    All 115 Value Lens images were downloaded via subagent using the same proven pattern and delivered to the Mac as
    9 zip parts (VL-p1.zip .. VL-p9.zip) inside /Users/office/School-of-Conscious-Communication/Values Cards/.
    THESE STILL NEED TO BE UNZIPPED, same as the Conversation Types and Choice Lenses zips above.

    Discovered this session: a Canva folder's lazy-loaded grid can get "stuck" partway through loading (scrollHeight
    stops growing well before all items are in the DOM) if you only call window.scrollTo() — this happened on the
    Values Cards folder, which stalled at 20/39/60/80/100 items across several plateaus. Fix: dispatch a synthetic
    WheelEvent (`document.body.dispatchEvent(new WheelEvent('wheel', {deltaY: 1200, bubbles: true, cancelable: true}))`)
    alongside the scrollTo call, as a SINGLE javascript_exec call per scroll step (not a multi-iteration loop in one
    call — loops longer than ~5-8 short iterations reliably hit the 45s CDP timeout on this folder for unclear
    reasons). Space consecutive single-step calls a couple seconds apart and re-check scrollHeight/get_page_text
    between them.

